+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` tracks a streak of consecutive losing trades - trades closing with a profit below `required_profit` (default `0.0`) - independent of the total profit or loss made. It ignores winning trades that may have happened earlier and only cares about what happened *in a row*, most recently first.
+
+Trades are considered per pair to determine `trade_limit`, or across all pairs simultaneously when evaluating the bot-wide (global) stop, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, in which case only the per-pair lock is used and the bot-wide lock is disabled.
+
+Once `trade_limit` losing trades have occurred back-to-back (for a pair, or bot-wide) within `lookback_period` (in minutes, or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), new entries for the affected pair (or all pairs, for the bot-wide streak) will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`). A single winning trade (or one with profit >= `required_profit`) resets the streak, and the cooldown is lifted automatically once `stop_duration` elapses - no manual intervention is required.
+
+As with other protections, `only_per_side` can be used on futures bots to track and lock only one side (long/short), letting the other side continue trading after a losing streak.
+
+The below example locks a pair for 4 candles after 3 consecutive losing trades on that same pair (looking back over the last 24 candles, and never triggering a bot-wide lock due to `only_per_pair`), and additionally halts all new entries bot-wide for 12 candles once 5 consecutive losing trades occur in a row across all pairs.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 3,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "only_per_pair": True,
+        },
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 24,
+            "trade_limit": 5,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 12,
+        },
+    ]
+```
+
+!!! Note
+    `trade_limit` and `lookback_period` will need to be tuned for your strategy. If `lookback_period` is too short, older trades that are part of the losing streak may fall out of the window before `trade_limit` is reached.
+
